From: FirebirdTA01 <FirebirdTA01@aol.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 19:30:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 39/39] spu: vmx2spu.h compiles in C++ (port of gcc-9.5.0 0005)

Fix unparenthesized compound literal in vec_sum2s macro invocation.

In C++ modes, commas inside unparenthesized compound literal braces
{0, -1, 0, -1} are treated by the preprocessor as macro argument separators,
causing `spu_and` to receive 5 arguments instead of 2.  Parenthesise the
compound literal as ((vec_int4){0, -1, 0, -1}), matching line 2262.

The restored backend takes vmx2spu.h unchanged from releases/gcc-9.5.0, so
the 9.5 fix applies here as is.
---
diff --git a/gcc/config/spu/vmx2spu.h b/gcc/config/spu/vmx2spu.h
--- a/gcc/config/spu/vmx2spu.h
+++ b/gcc/config/spu/vmx2spu.h
@@ -2215,7 +2215,7 @@
 
   sat = spu_orc(spu_xor(sign1, sign2), (vec_int4)spu_cmpeq(sum_h, sign2));
 
-  d = spu_and(spu_sel(sum_l, sat_val, (vec_uint4)(sat)), (vec_int4){0, -1, 0, -1});
+  d = spu_and(spu_sel(sum_l, sat_val, (vec_uint4)(sat)), ((vec_int4){0, -1, 0, -1}));
 
   return (d);
 }
